## Beyond the managed section

The managed `CLAUDE.md` section holds the addressing, body, comment and link rules. What it does
not say:

- Never hand-edit frontmatter or the `<!-- sq:* -->` markers; every region is written through a
  command.
- `--file -` reads a body or comment from stdin; `--desc` (on `create`/`update`) sets only the short
  summary shown in lists.
- Edit a sub-entity's metadata with `sq <type> <n> <kind> <k> update` (`--title`, `--status`,
  `--assignee`, plus any kind-declared fields{% if _kind_hints %} — e.g. {{ _kind_hints | join(', ') }}{% endif %}). Read it back with
  `sq <type> <n> <kind> <k> show`.
- Comment `edit` and `remove` take `--as <slug>` after the verb, like `-m` and `--file`.
- A hash quoted in prose pins the text its author read.

